"text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn8le15ob04re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 11, "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}]}, {"type": "audio", "_data": [], "title": "", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "image": "engenn8le15ob04re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "What do you know about genetic engineering? Genetics is a field of science. It studies how characteristics are passed on from parent to offspring. Genetic engineering investigates how genetics can be used and applied. <br/><br/>The best known area of genetic engineering is cloning. How can you describe cloning? Cloning produces a group of living things genetically identical to the parent. It's already a practical natural reproductive solution for some plants and animals.", "image": "engenn8le15ob04re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"text": "Why do scientists want to experiment with artificial cloning? What have they done so far in this area? In 1997, Scottish scientists made headlines when they successfully cloned a sheep using genetic material from a six-year-old ewe.\n<br/><br/>\nResearchers saw cloning endangered animals as the logical next step. Others were critical, viewing cloning as radical, immoral and impractical - the stuff of science fiction. Would you someday keep a personal clone? How would you feel when you used those clones for replacement parts?", "image": "engenn8le15ob04re2img02.jpg", "time": "29000", "id": 2}, {"text": "In reality, how far along have we actually come with cloning? To date, the failure rate with animals, which was supposed to be very low, is still very high. Plant cloning, on the other hand, is an economical way to produce uniform gardens with a consistent, equal growth rate.", "image": "engenn8le15ob04re2img03.jpg", "time": "62000", "id": 3}], "coverimg": "engenn8le15ob04re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le15ob04re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Science, Old and New", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Advances in Genetics", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "  Words Ending in Suffix <span class=\"italic\">-ical</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The suffix <span class=\"italic\">-ical</span> is used to transform nouns to adjectives.<br/> It means \"of or pertaining to\".", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "  Some of the examples of words ending in <span class=\"italic\">-ical</span> are: <br/>   <span class=\"italic\">mythical, chemical, alphabetical and technical.</span><br/><br/>You pronounce the suffix <span class=\"italic\">-ical</span> as \u201cicul\u201d", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice saying these words out loud:<br/><br/> identical<br/> practical<br/> artificial<br/> material<br/> logical<br/> critical<br/> radical<br/> impractical<br/> economical", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Cloning produces a group of living things genetically identical to the parent. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's already a practical natural reproductive solution for some plants and animals. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Why do scientists want to experiment with artificial cloning?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In 1997, Scottish scientists made headlines when they successfully cloned a sheep using genetic material from a six-year-old ewe. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Researchers saw cloning endangered animals as the logical next step. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Others were critical, viewing cloning as radical, immoral and impractical.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Plant cloning, on the other hand, is an economical way to produce uniform gardens.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Reduction of Auxiliary Verbs and Pronouns in Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you speak, it is common to use the reduced form of modals and auxiliaries in sentences and questions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Reduction is very common in conversations. It doesn't happen when you write. <br/>When you use a reduced form of auxiliary verbs in a questions, you link the words together when you say them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Examples: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">What do you mean? = <span class=\"strong\">Whatchu</span> mean?<br/> What do you know about genetic engineering? = <span class=\"strong\">Whatchu</span> know about genetic engineering? <br/> How would you feel when you used those clones for  replacement parts? = <span class=\"strong\">Howdjya</span> feel when you used those  clones for replacement parts?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use pronouns other than <span class=\"italic\">you</span>, the pronoun itself is not reduced, but is still part of the 3-word glide.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">What have they done so far in this area? = <span class=\"strong\">Whaduvthey</span> done so far in this area?  <br/>In reality, how far have we actually come with cloning? = In reality, how <span class=\"strong\">faruvwe</span> actually come with cloning? </span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to clone", "type": "name"}, {"content": "To make multiple identical copies of (a DNA sequence)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Genetic engineers clone a group of living things so they could be genetically identical to the parent.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about cloning.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "offspring", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the immediate descendant or descendants of a person, animal, etc.; progeny", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Genetics studies how characteristics are passed on from parent to offspring.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "genetic material", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the genetic composition of living organisms", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Scottish scientists made headlines when they successfully cloned a sheep using genetic material from a six-year-old ewe. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": " critical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "inclined to find fault or to judge with severity, often too readily", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some researchers were critical of cloning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "radical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "thoroughgoing or extreme, especially as regards change from accepted or traditional forms", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some researchers viewed cloning as radical. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "impractical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not practical or useful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cloning is viewed as an impractical procedure. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "immoral", "type": "name"}, {"content": "contrary to established moral principles", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some researchers, were critical viewing cloning as radical, immoral and impractical - the stuff of science fiction.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "economical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "designed or functioning to make effective use of money or effort invested", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Plant cloning is an economical way to produce uniform gardens.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Consider what it would mean if everyone could have a medical clone.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of pros and cons of this practice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Would they be human? Property? Where would they live?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What would the benefits be?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Where would they live?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Who would bring them up?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your list of pros and cons to another student.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to their ideas and discuss them all.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I list the pros and cons of cloning humans.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my list to a partner, paying careful attention to pronunciation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss my ideas and my partner's ideas.", "type": "text"}]}]}